                    'en' => [
                        'title' => 'Terms of Service',
                        'subtitle' => 'The legal agreement covering eligibility, listings, fees, payments and your rights on UniTill.',
                        'description' => json_encode([
                            "Definitions — Capitalised terms used in these Terms have the meanings given in Schedule 1 (Shared Definitions), covering terms such as Account, Buyer, Seller, Listing, Platform, Content, Guest and Student Verification.",
                            "About UNITILL LTD — The Platform is operated by UNITILL LTD, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 16970885, with its registered office at 53 Parkway Grange, Leeds, England, LS14 6UR; contact info@unitill.co.uk for general enquiries, complaints and privacy/data-protection enquiries.",
                            "Eligibility — UniTill is a student marketplace for current students of UK universities supported by UniTill; to create an Account you must successfully complete Student Verification using an eligible university-issued email address; UniTill may refuse registration or restrict access where a person cannot meet the Student Verification requirements.",
                            "Student Verification — Student Verification is completed using an eligible university-issued email address, checked against UniTill's approved UK university database; you must re-verify your student status every 12 months; if you can no longer re-verify because you have graduated or otherwise stopped being a current student, UniTill may provide a 60-day grace period during which you may manage existing listings and conversations but not create new listings; after the 60-day grace period, access to student-only features may be restricted unless you become eligible to re-verify; Student Verification confirms university affiliation only and does not guarantee another user's identity, honesty, reliability or the quality, safety or legality of anything they advertise.",
                            "Account Registration and Security — To use most features you must create an Account and provide accurate, current and complete information, and keep it up to date; you are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and for activity under your Account, and must contact info@unitill.co.uk promptly if you suspect unauthorised use; you must not share, sell or transfer your Account or create one on behalf of another person, as each Account is personal to the verified student who created it; UniTill may refuse registration, or warn, restrict, suspend or close an Account, where these Terms or policies have been breached, where required by law, or where necessary to protect the Platform or its users.",
                            "Guest Access — Guests may view limited information about public listings, including the listing title, price and images; full listing details, seller information, location information and messaging are available only to eligible signed-in users, and Guests cannot contact sellers or create listings.",
                            "Our Role as a Marketplace — UniTill provides a marketplace where verified students can advertise, discover and communicate about goods, accommodation and permitted services, and is not the buyer, seller, landlord, tenant or service provider in transactions between users; buyers and sellers arrange and complete payments directly between themselves, and UniTill does not process those user-to-user payments, provide seller payouts, escrow or buyer/seller payment protection; any agreement for goods, accommodation or services is made directly between the relevant users, and UniTill is not a party to it or an agent for either user; UniTill does not guarantee that a user, listing, item, accommodation or service is genuine, accurate, safe, suitable, available or lawful.",
                            "Buyer Responsibilities — Check the listing carefully and ask the seller any questions before agreeing to buy or arrange a service; inspect an item before paying where reasonably possible; agree payment, collection or delivery directly with the seller, as UniTill does not handle these payments; take reasonable safety precautions when meeting another user and follow the Community Guidelines; and report suspicious listings, scams or unsafe behaviour to UniTill.",
                            "Seller Responsibilities — Only list items, accommodation or services that you own, are authorised to offer, and are legally allowed on UniTill; describe what you are offering honestly and accurately, using genuine photos and clearly disclosing important faults or defects; set an accurate price and location; follow the Prohibited & Restricted Items Policy and Community Guidelines; deal fairly with other users and honour what you advertise; understand and meet any tax or other legal obligations that apply to your own sales or services; and do not use UniTill as a business, company, shop or professional trader storefront, though a verified student may advertise permitted services in a personal capacity under Section 13.",
                            "Listing Creation and Publication — When creating a Listing you must choose the correct category, provide the required information and pay any applicable Listing fee before publication; draft Listings are free and a Listing fee is charged only when you choose to publish; UniTill may review, reject, hide or remove a Listing if it reasonably believes it breaches these Terms, the Prohibited & Restricted Items Policy, the Community Guidelines or the law, or is in the wrong category; publication does not mean UniTill has checked, approved or endorsed the item, accommodation, service or seller; a published Listing remains live for 30 days unless marked as sold or removed earlier, and an eligible expired Listing may be extended for a further 30 days for £0.99.",
                            "Car Listings — UniTill may use an approved vehicle-data provider to retrieve basic vehicle information from the registration mark you enter, and you are responsible for checking that information is correct and completing any missing details; you may only list a vehicle you are legally entitled to sell and hold the relevant documentation for; Vehicle Listings must comply with the Prohibited & Restricted Items Policy, including rules against cloned vehicles, false mileage, misleading information and vehicles being presented as roadworthy when they are not; you must not use another vehicle's registration mark or enter registration details for any unrelated purpose.",
                            "Accommodation Listings — You may only advertise genuine accommodation you are legally entitled to let, sublet, assign or otherwise offer; you must provide accurate information about the accommodation, price, availability and any important conditions, and comply with any housing, tenancy, licensing, safety and non-discrimination requirements that apply; UniTill may display an approximate location rather than the precise address to help protect users' privacy, and you are responsible for ensuring the location information you provide is accurate.",
                            "Services Listings — Students may advertise ordinary services such as tutoring, cleaning, photography, translation, design, basic technology help and similar services, provided independently and not as an employee, agent, partner or representative of UniTill; you are responsible for providing the service safely, honestly and lawfully; you must not advertise a regulated or high-risk service unless specifically permitted, including services requiring professional licences such as certain medical, legal, financial, childcare, gas or electrical services; academic cheating services are prohibited, while legitimate tutoring, proofreading and study support are allowed provided the service does not involve completing work for someone to submit as their own.",
                            "Listing Fees and Payments — The Listing fees are: Standard Listing £0.99, Car Listing £2.99, Accommodation Listing £2.99, and a 30-day Listing extension £0.99; drafts are free and you are charged only when you choose to publish or extend a Listing; the price shown before payment is the total price payable including any applicable taxes; UniTill may change its prices in future, but a price change will not affect a Listing or extension you have already paid for; UniTill may offer discount or promotional codes, which have no cash value and may be refused or cancelled if used fraudulently; payment is handled through the method shown at checkout, and UniTill does not process payments between buyers and sellers for the goods, accommodation or services advertised.",
                            "Cancellations and Refunds — When you purchase a paid Listing or extension, you can ask UniTill to start the service immediately by selecting \"Start my listing immediately\" before payment; if you have a legal right to cancel within 14 days and asked us to start the service during that period, we may deduct a reasonable amount for the service already supplied, as permitted by law; selling an item quickly, changing your mind, or no longer needing the Listing does not by itself give an additional right to a refund; if UniTill fails to publish a paid Listing, or removes it because of a problem caused by UniTill, we may provide an appropriate refund or credit; we will not normally refund a Listing removed because the user breached these Terms, the Community Guidelines, the Prohibited & Restricted Items Policy or the law; to cancel where you have a legal cancellation right, use any cancellation option in the Platform or email info@unitill.co.uk.",
                            "Messaging and User Communication — UniTill provides in-app messaging so verified users can communicate about Listings and services; you must use messaging only for genuine and lawful purposes, as harassment, threats, scams, spam, illegal content and misuse of personal information are prohibited; UniTill may access, retain or review messages where reasonably necessary to operate the Platform, investigate reports, protect users, enforce our rules or comply with the law.",
                            "Reports, Complaints and Appeals — Users can report Listings, messages, users or other Content that they believe breaks our rules or the law; UniTill may review a report and take appropriate action, including removing Content, warning a user, restricting features, suspending an Account or closing an Account; if you are unhappy with a decision, you may submit a complaint or appeal through the contact method shown in the Platform or by emailing info@unitill.co.uk; where we take action against your Account or Content, we will normally explain the reason and give you an opportunity to appeal, unless doing so would be unsafe or legally inappropriate.",
                            "Moderation and Content Removal — UniTill may review, restrict, hide or remove Listings, messages, profiles or other Content that we reasonably believe breaks our Terms, policies or the law, and will take proportionate steps to remove illegal Content swiftly as required by law; we may use reports from users, automated tools and human review to help identify suspicious, harmful or prohibited Content; where appropriate, UniTill may take action against the responsible Account, including a warning, feature restriction, suspension or permanent closure; users can challenge eligible moderation decisions through the complaints and appeals process.",
                            "Account Restrictions, Closure and Deletion — You may deactivate your Account temporarily or permanently delete it using the options provided in the Platform, or by contacting info@unitill.co.uk; deactivation temporarily disables your Account and is reversible, and does not permanently delete your data; permanent deletion removes your active Listings and Account access and starts deletion of associated personal data, subject to limited retention where necessary for legal, fraud-prevention, safety, moderation, dispute or regulatory reasons; deactivating, closing or permanently deleting your Account does not automatically entitle you to a refund of fees already paid, except where the Cancellations and Refunds section or the law gives that right; UniTill may warn, restrict, suspend or permanently close an Account where these Terms or policies are breached, where necessary to protect users or the Platform, where required by law, or where student eligibility can no longer be verified, including after the 60-day grace period.",
                            "Intellectual Property and User Content — UniTill owns or licenses the Platform, including its software, design, text, graphics, logos and branding, which you may use only for its intended purpose; you keep ownership of the Content you upload, including Listing text and photographs; by uploading Content you give UniTill a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, store, display, reproduce and format it as reasonably necessary to operate the Platform, show your Listings and comply with the law; you confirm you own the Content or have permission to use it, and that it does not infringe another person's intellectual-property rights; if someone believes Content on UniTill infringes their rights, they can contact UniTill and we may review or remove it where appropriate.",
                            "Platform Availability — We try to keep UniTill available and working properly, but cannot guarantee the Platform will always be available, uninterrupted or free from errors; we may temporarily suspend, restrict or change all or part of the Platform for maintenance, security, technical, legal or operational reasons, and will give notice of significant planned interruptions where reasonably possible; UniTill is intended for personal student use, and business, company, shop or professional trader storefronts are not currently supported.",
                            "Disclaimers and Liability — Nothing in these Terms limits any responsibility UniTill cannot legally limit, including your statutory consumer rights; UniTill provides the marketplace but is not the buyer, seller, landlord, tenant or service provider in transactions between users, and is not responsible for another user's actions, statements, Listings, goods, accommodation or services where the loss was not caused by UniTill; UniTill does not guarantee that a user, Listing, item, accommodation or service is genuine, accurate, safe, suitable or available, as Student Verification confirms university affiliation only; we are not responsible for losses that were not reasonably foreseeable or that result from events outside our reasonable control; UniTill remains responsible where the law requires, including for providing its own paid services with reasonable care and skill.",
                            "Your Consumer Rights — Nothing in these Terms affects any rights you have under UK consumer law; UniTill's own paid services, such as paid Listings and extensions, must be provided with reasonable care and skill; where the law gives you cancellation rights for a paid UniTill service, those rights apply as explained in the Cancellations and Refunds section.",
                            "Changes to the Platform and Terms — UniTill may update these Terms or its policies where necessary because of changes to the Platform, its services, its business or the law; when a significant change is made, UniTill will take reasonable steps to tell users, for example through the app or by email; updated Terms will show a new effective date, and changes will not normally affect fees already paid or purchases made under an earlier version; if a change requires you to accept new Terms before continuing to use UniTill, you will be asked to do so.",
                            "Governing Law and Jurisdiction — These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales; if you are a consumer living elsewhere in the UK, you keep any mandatory legal rights and protections that apply to you; nothing in these Terms is intended to prevent you from using any court or dispute route that the law says must remain available to you.",
